Provides two functions fancycut and wafflecut, which essentially do the same thing, with slightly different syntax.
These function allow for turning a numeric vector into a factor, like base cut
However, unlike base cut, they give the user more control over how to specify the intervals.
The intervals can be a mix of open/close, close/open, etc.
The function also allows trivial intervals, i.e. points, to be mapped to a factor level.
Additionally, it is OK if some values don't map to any buckets, and the user can specify an unmatched bucket.
